# Force LF everywhere. The harness generates shell scripts, Dockerfiles and
# entrypoints that run inside Linux containers: a CRLF shebang makes the kernel
# look for a binary literally named "/bin/sh\r" and fails with
#   exec /entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
# while the file is plainly there. Checking out CRLF on a Windows clone would
# reintroduce that, so normalise on the way in and out.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never let these be converted, under any core.autocrlf setting.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.mjs     text eol=lf
*.js      text eol=lf
*.ts      text eol=lf
*.tsx     text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
